WEBVTT

00:00:01.730 --> 00:00:05.930
All right, now that the 
class trip is behind us...

00:00:05.930 --> 00:00:08.170
Ayase-san, since you want 
to become a teacher...

00:00:09.020 --> 00:00:12.500
Exactly what subject
 are you hoping to teach?

00:00:19.220 --> 00:00:21.770
Well, if we go by your grades,

00:00:21.770 --> 00:00:24.750
you're far more suited to 
PE than anything else.

00:00:25.270 --> 00:00:27.130
But Ms. Miyauchi...

00:00:27.130 --> 00:00:30.130
<b>PE</b>

00:00:27.130 --> 00:00:30.130
Make sure she picks a subject 
where students don't die!

00:00:30.130 --> 00:00:32.550
...said that to me.

00:00:36.270 --> 00:00:40.020
Well, let's take a little more time 
to think about it, shall we?

00:00:41.970 --> 00:00:47.140
<b><i>Chihayafuru 3</i></b>

00:00:47.140 --> 00:00:48.970
<b><i>Chihayafuru 3</i></b>

00:01:52.710 --> 00:01:57.630
Verse 11

00:01:52.710 --> 00:01:57.630
Leaving a 
hovering 
mist 
above the 
trees and
 grass

00:01:57.630 --> 00:01:59.260
<b><i>Competitive
Karuta Club
New members always welcome!</i></b>

00:02:02.520 --> 00:02:06.510
<i>Mashima's clearly been off his game
since the qualifiers,</i>

00:02:06.510 --> 00:02:10.190
<i>and Ayase's still riding the momentum 
from her win at the Yoshino Tournament.</i>

00:02:10.190 --> 00:02:12.780
<i>She's not holding anything back, either.</i>

00:02:14.720 --> 00:02:16.380
Thank you very much.

00:02:16.380 --> 00:02:18.540
<i>She won by 20 cards!</i>

00:02:18.540 --> 00:02:22.730
<i>Ayase! He's never gonna 
bounce back that way!</i>

00:02:29.370 --> 00:02:31.600
<i>I don't know what I'm supposed to do,</i>

00:02:32.340 --> 00:02:34.760
<i>or how to make him feel better.</i>

00:02:35.900 --> 00:02:38.190
<i>But if I hold anything back...</i>

00:02:38.190 --> 00:02:40.040
<i>If I don't play with my full strength...</i>

00:02:40.660 --> 00:02:43.330
<i>I get the feeling he'll 
just stop playing karuta.</i>

00:02:46.210 --> 00:02:47.640
I'll be the reader next.

00:02:48.880 --> 00:02:50.470
We'll start in ten minutes.

00:02:51.180 --> 00:02:54.220
By the way, Ayase,
 did you call Wataya Arata?

00:02:54.220 --> 00:02:56.260
Huh? No.

00:02:56.260 --> 00:02:57.580
Well, call him!

00:02:57.580 --> 00:03:01.720
He's the youngest male West 
representative ever! That's a big deal!

00:03:12.790 --> 00:03:15.020
No. I'll call him later.

00:03:15.760 --> 00:03:19.000
Speak of the devil! Is that 
a message from Wataya?

00:03:19.000 --> 00:03:20.360
Oh, I got one, too.

00:03:20.360 --> 00:03:21.380
Me, too.

00:03:21.180 --> 00:03:21.760
<b>From Wataya?</b>

00:03:23.800 --> 00:03:30.060
To all Shiranami Society ML members 

00:03:38.300 --> 00:03:39.390
Taichi?

00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:43.100
Nah, it's nothing. Let's go.

00:03:45.650 --> 00:03:48.120
<i>Do I have to go?</i>

00:03:48.570 --> 00:03:50.030
<i>I don't want to.</i>

00:03:50.450 --> 00:03:53.760
<i>I can't face Dr. Harada right now.</i>

00:03:56.910 --> 00:03:59.670
I called you all here today for one reason:

00:04:00.030 --> 00:04:02.850
to announce my plan for producing
the Shiranami Society's first Master,

00:04:02.850 --> 00:04:05.690
my greatest dream since the day 
this society was founded!

00:04:05.680 --> 00:04:07.680
<b>Announce...</b>

00:04:06.060 --> 00:04:07.690
<i>Announce?</i>

00:04:07.960 --> 00:04:10.440
We have one month until 
the East-West Playoff!

00:04:10.440 --> 00:04:12.690
We can't waste a single day!

00:04:13.000 --> 00:04:14.690
First, you Class A kids!

00:04:15.010 --> 00:04:18.230
You will participate more 
proactively than ever in practice

00:04:18.230 --> 00:04:23.010
and challenge me as if you were competing 
to be Master or Queen yourself!

00:04:23.010 --> 00:04:24.690
Those of you in Class B and below

00:04:24.690 --> 00:04:28.140
will devote yourselves to strategy 
formulation and self-discipline

00:04:28.140 --> 00:04:31.200
and heighten the competitive 
atmosphere of our practices!

00:04:31.550 --> 00:04:33.340
For my sake!

00:04:34.260 --> 00:04:37.490
<i>Dr. Harada's finally letting 
his true motives take over.</i>

00:04:37.250 --> 00:04:45.470
<b>Bam</b>

00:04:38.640 --> 00:04:43.030
<i>I started the Shiranami Society so 
that I could become Master one day.</i>

00:04:43.030 --> 00:04:46.870
<i>It's to make myself stronger
that I guide the younger players, too!</i>

00:04:47.560 --> 00:04:50.510
Tsuboguchi-kun, you're free 
to coach your own students,

00:04:50.510 --> 00:04:52.480
but you have to come here 
at least twice a week!

00:04:52.480 --> 00:04:54.070
Wow, that'll be rough.

00:04:54.070 --> 00:04:55.360
As for you, Eyelashes...

00:04:55.350 --> 00:05:00.320
Wataya Arata's Preferred Layout

00:04:56.410 --> 00:05:01.030
Tsuboguchi-kun and Hanano-san made me 
this chart of Glasses' card layout.

00:05:01.730 --> 00:05:03.630
Use this to play against me!

00:05:01.730 --> 00:05:06.320
<i>Wataya Arata's Preferred Layout</i>

00:05:04.110 --> 00:05:05.980
<i>Arata's card layout?</i>

00:05:06.580 --> 00:05:09.370
<i>I'm supposed to be a virtual Arata?</i>

00:05:10.500 --> 00:05:12.570
I... I can't do that.

00:05:12.890 --> 00:05:16.810
Suddenly playing with someone else's layout
won't make me a good training dummy.

00:05:16.810 --> 00:05:17.450
<i>I won't.</i>

00:05:17.450 --> 00:05:18.960
What are you talking about?!

00:05:18.960 --> 00:05:22.180
You still played well after changing 
your own placement like that!

00:05:21.880 --> 00:05:23.840
<b>You're versatile enough</b>

00:05:22.180 --> 00:05:23.950
You're the only one who <i>can</i> do this!

00:05:23.950 --> 00:05:26.530
Even if I copy Arata,
I can't play like him!

00:05:26.530 --> 00:05:27.350
<i>I won't!</i>

00:05:28.160 --> 00:05:31.520
You're the one who made me
the East Japan representative!

00:05:38.600 --> 00:05:39.920
I yield this match.

00:05:39.920 --> 00:05:42.870
He claimed he'd jammed his finger,

00:05:42.870 --> 00:05:45.760
but the reason Sudo-kun 
yielded to me in the finals

00:05:45.760 --> 00:05:48.610
was clearly because of his wager with you!

00:05:48.980 --> 00:05:51.140
Of course, I would've 
won if I'd played him,

00:05:51.140 --> 00:05:53.370
but I got out of hurting 
my knee any further!

00:05:54.080 --> 00:05:57.710
The fight Tsuboguchi-kun put up
in the semifinals helped,

00:05:57.710 --> 00:06:01.530
but your strength at the 
Yoshino Tournament saved me, too!

00:06:02.510 --> 00:06:03.890
I want...

00:06:03.890 --> 00:06:07.700
to fight with the help of everyone 
in the Shiranami Society!

00:06:07.700 --> 00:06:11.640
Being on the receiving end of 
that help makes me stronger!

00:06:20.910 --> 00:06:22.200
<i>Full strength...</i>

00:06:23.050 --> 00:06:25.190
<i>Dr. Harada's full strength...</i>

00:06:27.150 --> 00:06:30.560
<i>pulls in everything around 
him to move him forward.</i>

00:06:33.240 --> 00:06:36.350
Dr. Harada, I'll memorize a layout, too.

00:06:36.350 --> 00:06:38.100
You don't need to do that.

00:06:37.830 --> 00:06:39.790
<b>You're not that versatile</b>

00:06:38.100 --> 00:06:39.800
You'll wreck your own play style.

00:06:40.360 --> 00:06:42.050
Not Arata's layout.

00:06:42.450 --> 00:06:44.020
Master Suo's.

00:06:45.740 --> 00:06:47.380
You have twenty!

00:06:47.380 --> 00:06:49.140
Twenty one-syllable cards!

00:06:51.130 --> 00:06:53.810
<i>A virtual Suo Hisashi...</i>

00:07:00.720 --> 00:07:01.770
<i>He's good.</i>

00:07:03.090 --> 00:07:06.890
<i>He's able to relax again,
 and he's tenacious on top of that.</i>

00:07:08.390 --> 00:07:11.320
<i>Nobody can call this the dumb luck of youth.</i>

00:07:12.910 --> 00:07:14.580
Okay, break time.

00:07:22.270 --> 00:07:23.010
Hello?

00:07:23.010 --> 00:07:25.580
<i>Congrats on becoming
the West Japan representative!</i>

00:07:27.340 --> 00:07:29.260
<b>Riiiing</b>

00:07:29.670 --> 00:07:33.360
Chihaya... That seriously 
threw my senses off.

00:07:33.360 --> 00:07:34.780
<i>What?! Really?!</i>

00:07:35.250 --> 00:07:37.800
Nah. I'm fine.

00:07:37.800 --> 00:07:38.740
<i>Arata!</i>

00:07:38.740 --> 00:07:41.850
The Shiranami Society's going 
to do all it can to beat you!

00:07:41.850 --> 00:07:45.270
The one who's going to Omi Jingu as
the challenger is Dr. Harada for sure!

00:07:46.070 --> 00:07:47.660
He's 100% not gonna lose!

00:07:47.650 --> 00:07:50.780
<b>Win                               Win</b>

00:07:47.660 --> 00:07:50.770
He's going to beat you!
Dr. Harada's going to win!

00:07:50.770 --> 00:07:53.670
He won't lose! He'll win for sure!

00:07:53.670 --> 00:07:57.050
The Shiranami Society's 
the best! We won't lose!

00:07:56.200 --> 00:07:57.910
Chihaya, you're such a pest.

00:07:57.050 --> 00:07:59.650
We're gonna win! The Shiranami 
Society's the best—

00:08:01.640 --> 00:08:04.130
You do your best too, Arata.

00:08:15.540 --> 00:08:17.920
<i>When I must hide...</i>

00:08:17.920 --> 00:08:19.810
<i>For most players, there are only</i>

00:08:19.810 --> 00:08:22.900
<i>seven one-syllable cards: "Rain, Silent, 
Long, Gust, All, Look, Swift."</i>

00:08:22.900 --> 00:08:25.980
<i>But in our interview, the 
Master had this to say.</i>

00:08:25.520 --> 00:08:31.650
<i>Suo Hisashi's Preferred Layout</i>

00:08:26.670 --> 00:08:30.200
<i>There are 28 one-syllable cards for him.</i>

00:08:34.470 --> 00:08:37.140
Come on, Chihaya! Give it a rest already!

00:08:37.140 --> 00:08:40.240
Let me check out the late 
night drama I was... in...

00:08:43.120 --> 00:08:44.670
<i>Suo Hisashi's Preferred Layout</i>

00:08:55.880 --> 00:08:58.610
<i>There are 28 one-syllable cards.</i>

00:09:00.780 --> 00:09:02.620
<i>28 cards...</i>

00:09:05.690 --> 00:09:08.060
<i>For the cold nights...</i>

00:09:10.760 --> 00:09:12.850
<i>I wish I could show...</i>

00:09:15.610 --> 00:09:21.110
<i>have been soaked red with tears of blood</i>

00:09:21.890 --> 00:09:24.270
<i>The storm blasts...</i>

00:09:24.830 --> 00:09:27.580
<i>Orange {top}</i>

00:09:24.830 --> 00:09:27.580
<i>100% Fruit Juice</i>

00:09:25.190 --> 00:09:27.590
This brings back memories.

00:09:28.170 --> 00:09:30.760
But you haven't gotten rusty 
at all, Sakurazawa-san.

00:09:30.760 --> 00:09:34.640
I guess practicing with high school kids
 every day helps, huh?

00:09:34.640 --> 00:09:36.210
What are you talking about?

00:09:36.530 --> 00:09:39.300
I'm hopeless. I've lost my tenacity.

00:09:39.300 --> 00:09:41.010
I practice too much.

00:09:42.190 --> 00:09:46.360
For veterans, one real match is
more important than ten practice games.

00:09:46.360 --> 00:09:49.110
You just beat me, though!

00:09:47.650 --> 00:09:49.100
<b>You got me good</b>

00:09:50.430 --> 00:09:54.440
Any game I play against you
is a "real match" for me.

00:09:57.440 --> 00:09:59.580
Okay, you're next, Rion. Go on.

00:10:02.300 --> 00:10:03.850
Hyuga-kun, you're the reader.

00:10:03.850 --> 00:10:04.620
Got it!

00:10:04.920 --> 00:10:07.270
<i>That's just mean, Coach Sakurazawa!</i>

00:10:07.270 --> 00:10:10.000
<i>I lost big time in the East Japan qualifiers!</i>

00:10:10.000 --> 00:10:12.840
<i>I couldn't make up for that minuscule 
difference in our game senses!</i>

00:10:13.330 --> 00:10:17.970
With Hyuga-kun's sloppy reading,
you might be able to beat me, Rion-chan.

00:10:19.230 --> 00:10:22.370
Though I wouldn't lose if we had 
the grade 7 Yamashiro as reader.

00:10:25.480 --> 00:10:26.590
Excuse me.

00:10:37.660 --> 00:10:39.360
Thank you for the game.

00:10:39.730 --> 00:10:46.500
<i>Naniwa Bay, now the flower 
blooms, but for winter</i>

00:10:42.420 --> 00:10:44.240
<i>Cheers, you suck at this!</i>

00:10:45.920 --> 00:10:48.000
<i>Way to egg her on, Inokuma-san.</i>

00:10:49.240 --> 00:10:51.730
<i>My Yamashiro's a fine raw 
gemstone, isn't she?</i>

00:10:52.280 --> 00:10:54.170
<i>You can tell she'll only go 
up from here, can't you?</i>

00:10:58.240 --> 00:10:59.680
<i>I noticed it earlier, too...</i>

00:11:00.600 --> 00:11:05.050
<i>but Inokuma-san's game sense isn't the same
as when she was in her prime.</i>

00:11:06.950 --> 00:11:10.780
<i>It peaks in a player's teens 
and early twenties.</i>

00:11:12.200 --> 00:11:13.850
<i>It's all downhill from there.</i>

00:11:19.010 --> 00:11:21.860
Thanks for the ride, Sakurazawa-san.

00:11:21.860 --> 00:11:24.010
It can't be easy,
 taking the bullet train here.

00:11:24.010 --> 00:11:25.290
Will you make it back next week?

00:11:25.290 --> 00:11:26.980
Sure, if you don't mind.

00:11:32.240 --> 00:11:33.300
<i>Shoot...</i>

00:11:33.300 --> 00:11:36.720
<i>Breast pump time. I'm tight as a drum.</i>

00:11:36.720 --> 00:11:40.690
<i>I guess nursing babies and their mommies
are made to never be apart.</i>

00:11:45.180 --> 00:11:50.060
<b>From: Inokuma Satoshi 

00:11:45.850 --> 00:11:46.910
<i>What?!</i>

00:11:46.910 --> 00:11:50.050
<i>Jin... has a fever?</i>

00:11:53.060 --> 00:11:56.570
<b>He's fine, but he's
 crying for his mama. 
Try to come 
home soon.</b>

00:12:12.080 --> 00:12:15.060
<i>The West representative, 
Ousaka-san, is 18 years old.</i>

00:12:15.550 --> 00:12:17.960
<i>The current Queen is 17.</i>

00:12:19.250 --> 00:12:23.330
<i>How am I supposed to win at the age of 34?</i>

00:12:27.610 --> 00:12:31.300
<i>Is that... more important than my children?</i>

00:12:33.800 --> 00:12:36.520
Chihaya! Your mom's serious now!

00:12:36.860 --> 00:12:39.250
I'm serious about supporting your dream!

00:12:40.160 --> 00:12:41.920
This is your cousin, Shinji-kun!

00:12:41.400 --> 00:12:42.570
Tweak Tweak

00:12:41.920 --> 00:12:45.420
He stopped by on his way home 
from work to help you study!

00:12:46.200 --> 00:12:48.670
I helped with your high school 
entrance exams, too.

00:12:48.670 --> 00:12:49.820
I hope you're grown a bit since...

00:12:51.380 --> 00:12:52.330
...then?!

00:12:51.540 --> 00:12:52.330
<b>Ba dump</b>

00:12:52.340 --> 00:12:55.700
I appreciate your help, Shinji.

00:12:57.140 --> 00:12:59.720
Has your voice gotten quieter, Chihaya-chan?

00:12:59.720 --> 00:13:01.260
This is just how it is.

00:13:01.260 --> 00:13:04.630
<b>Tweak Tweak Tweak Tweak</b>

00:13:01.570 --> 00:13:04.630
<i>I-Is it... a signal to move closer?</i>

00:13:05.090 --> 00:13:08.460
O-Okay, then. I'll have to sit next to you.

00:13:08.460 --> 00:13:10.510
Would you like some sweets?

00:13:11.630 --> 00:13:13.960
<i>Is this... a sign of love?!</i>

00:13:17.030 --> 00:13:21.030
Dr. Harada told President Mashima to 
memorize Wataya-san's card placement?!

00:13:21.410 --> 00:13:25.090
That's just rubbing salt in his wound!

00:13:25.090 --> 00:13:26.370
I know, right?

00:13:26.370 --> 00:13:28.850
And Mashima's just as messed up
for actually doing it!

00:13:28.850 --> 00:13:30.770
Not that I didn't know it, 
but he's a total masochist!

00:13:31.020 --> 00:13:33.840
Stop talking about the Shiranami Society!

00:13:31.200 --> 00:13:34.910
<b>Trying to memorize this</b>

00:13:33.840 --> 00:13:34.910
What's up with you guys?

00:13:37.490 --> 00:13:40.120
<i>He generally keeps similar cards separated.</i>

00:13:40.520 --> 00:13:43.600
<i>He keeps "Long" and "Rain" split 
between left and right, too.</i>

00:13:44.230 --> 00:13:46.540
<i>His cross is incredible.</i>

00:13:47.240 --> 00:13:48.520
<i>Cross...</i>

00:13:50.300 --> 00:13:52.380
Okay, today's first matches are...

00:13:52.730 --> 00:13:57.130
Mashima and Ayase, Tsukuba and Kana-chan,
and Hanano-san and me.

00:13:57.130 --> 00:13:58.420
Porky will be the reader.

00:13:58.560 --> 00:13:59.560
<b>Manju</b>

00:13:59.560 --> 00:14:01.740
What? You're giving that to me?

00:14:01.740 --> 00:14:03.610
I can't, because you're not in Class A.

00:14:03.610 --> 00:14:04.360
Huh?!

00:14:03.650 --> 00:14:04.360
<b>Shock</b>

00:14:04.360 --> 00:14:06.650
<i>Whaaaa...</i>

00:14:04.550 --> 00:14:06.650
<i>She's imitating Suo Hisashi?!</i>

00:14:07.040 --> 00:14:09.280
<i>What do we do about this?</i>

00:14:09.280 --> 00:14:10.940
<i>We have an idiot among us!</i>

00:14:11.710 --> 00:14:13.680
Are you in Class A?

00:14:13.680 --> 00:14:14.910
No, I'm not!

00:14:17.150 --> 00:14:19.180
L-Let's play some karuta, eh?

00:14:19.180 --> 00:14:20.540
<i>And another idiot!</i>

00:14:19.250 --> 00:14:20.540
<b><i>What?!</i></b>

00:14:23.000 --> 00:14:24.630
<i>How will this go, though?</i>

00:14:25.260 --> 00:14:29.200
<i>One's trying to be Suo Hisashi,
and one's trying to be Wataya Arata.</i>

00:14:30.130 --> 00:14:35.090
<i>...now the flower blooms</i>

00:14:37.140 --> 00:14:39.340
<i>Feel sorrow wash over me...</i>

00:14:40.510 --> 00:14:42.750
<i>She put "Feel love" and "Feel sorrow"
beside each other</i>

00:14:42.750 --> 00:14:44.480
<i>and held them down together.</i>

00:14:45.310 --> 00:14:48.610
<i>If someone with good game sense pulls that 
on you, there's nothing you can do.</i>

00:14:49.460 --> 00:14:52.250
<i>She's even imitating how often 
he holds cards down.</i>

00:14:53.220 --> 00:14:54.890
<i>Same for everything else.</i>

00:14:54.890 --> 00:14:57.430
<i>She put the cards she's 
confident in close together</i>

00:14:57.430 --> 00:14:59.790
<i>so she can win them before 
they're even read.</i>

00:15:00.380 --> 00:15:02.880
<i>That's not easy, even if you 
understand the concept!</i>

00:15:02.880 --> 00:15:04.900
<i>You're amazing, Ayase!</i>

00:15:06.530 --> 00:15:10.280
<i>Pursue the world seen 
through Suo-san's eyes.</i>

00:15:11.350 --> 00:15:14.340
<i>Seen? Heard?</i>

00:15:16.160 --> 00:15:16.970
<i>Damn it!</i>

00:15:17.640 --> 00:15:20.560
<i>It must be nice to be able to do that.</i>

00:15:20.560 --> 00:15:23.930
<i>It's taking all I have just 
to not feel discouraged.</i>

00:15:24.690 --> 00:15:25.850
<i>Wait, no...</i>

00:15:25.850 --> 00:15:27.510
It's taking all I have.

00:15:28.150 --> 00:15:29.110
<b>He'd never say that</b>

00:15:29.900 --> 00:15:32.240
<i>Arata would never say that.</i>

00:15:33.100 --> 00:15:36.720
<i>It's difficult to achieve a 
similar level of game sense,</i>

00:15:36.720 --> 00:15:39.110
<i>but there are plenty of other 
ways to take cards faster.</i>

00:15:40.260 --> 00:15:42.110
<i>Would this old...</i>

00:15:43.350 --> 00:15:45.130
That was pretty ugly, Mashima.

00:15:44.380 --> 00:15:46.340
<b>Ugly?!</b>

00:15:45.130 --> 00:15:46.330
But you used a cross to take that!

00:15:47.360 --> 00:15:50.340
Ayase went straight for 
the "Would this" card,

00:15:50.340 --> 00:15:53.440
but you were prepared to take both 
"Would this" and "Would the"

00:15:53.440 --> 00:15:55.670
so you could win it on the first syllable!

00:15:56.070 --> 00:16:00.320
Is the cross stroke a way to play on equal
footing as players with good game sense?

00:16:00.320 --> 00:16:01.560
With some refining, it is.

00:16:02.400 --> 00:16:05.670
<i>What Arata refines...</i>

00:16:07.300 --> 00:16:09.770
<i>He does this at such insane 
speeds right from the start.</i>

00:16:10.420 --> 00:16:14.000
<i>It's not like the fundamental rule 
of listening with your hands.</i>

00:16:15.080 --> 00:16:18.000
<i>This is hard. It's a weapon 
of a different type.</i>

00:16:20.270 --> 00:16:22.780
But after one "Would" card is read,
you can't do it again!

00:16:22.780 --> 00:16:24.950
I'll get the next one! Just watch!

00:16:23.080 --> 00:16:23.870
<b>Ah...</b>

00:16:23.870 --> 00:16:24.960
<b>Ah...  She's back...</b>

00:16:26.630 --> 00:16:28.710
I'll... get the next one.

00:16:27.420 --> 00:16:28.710
<b>Is that how
 Suo-san acts?</b>

00:16:29.500 --> 00:16:33.960
And after I win my fifth 
consecutive title, I'll retire.

00:16:37.100 --> 00:16:39.470
<b>Fuchu City Katamachi Cultural Center</b>

00:16:40.980 --> 00:16:48.480
<i>Wataya Arata's Preferred Layout</i>

00:16:41.610 --> 00:16:45.770
So Glasses keeps "Since the" and "Since I" 
split up between left and right

00:16:45.770 --> 00:16:48.490
and always uses a cross for them...

00:16:48.490 --> 00:16:52.550
Even if they're separated, I think he'd 
put them here to make you aim for them.

00:16:52.970 --> 00:16:55.280
Especially "Since the," in this case.

00:16:55.280 --> 00:16:59.030
But I think that means he's sure he can 
always take them, no matter what.

00:16:59.030 --> 00:17:01.840
That definitely makes me 
want to take them myself.

00:17:02.160 --> 00:17:03.470
And Suo-kun?

00:17:03.470 --> 00:17:06.000
He moves forward softly 
and takes cards swiftly.

00:17:06.000 --> 00:17:07.600
He holds cards down a lot.

00:17:07.600 --> 00:17:10.090
Yes, I can see that much by watching him.

00:17:08.170 --> 00:17:10.090
<b>Everyone 
knows that</b>

00:17:13.850 --> 00:17:16.370
Okay, that's it for today.

00:17:18.960 --> 00:17:22.020
<i>The challenger playoff is 
already this weekend...</i>

00:17:22.690 --> 00:17:26.170
Thank you both, Eyelashes and Chihaya-chan.

00:17:26.170 --> 00:17:28.340
This has been great practice.

00:17:28.770 --> 00:17:32.360
Um, Dr. Harada... Could 
it be that Master Suo...

00:17:34.230 --> 00:17:35.880
N-Never mind.

00:17:36.410 --> 00:17:39.170
You're an odd girl, Chihaya-chan.

00:17:37.070 --> 00:17:41.240
<b>And a-hup</b>

00:17:39.170 --> 00:17:41.220
What's that you're doing?

00:17:49.960 --> 00:17:54.470
November 24th 
Otsuka Karuta 
Memorial Hall

00:17:49.960 --> 00:17:54.470
Master and Queen
 Challenger Playoffs

00:17:58.570 --> 00:18:00.470
Megumu's so cute!

00:18:00.140 --> 00:18:05.100
<b>Click Click Click Click Click</b>

00:18:00.470 --> 00:18:03.150
Megumu-tan, you're cosmically cute!

00:18:03.150 --> 00:18:05.110
You guys busted out the headbands...

00:18:07.690 --> 00:18:10.090
It's been ages since I wore a hakama.

00:18:10.090 --> 00:18:14.230
I'd love to cheer you on, but Aki 
and Jin would make too much noise.

00:18:14.230 --> 00:18:16.230
I'll take them to the park or something.

00:18:17.410 --> 00:18:19.730
Will you come to the park with us, Mommy?

00:18:19.730 --> 00:18:20.730
Will you?

00:18:26.100 --> 00:18:28.660
What's wrong, Jin? Need to nurse?

00:18:28.660 --> 00:18:31.910
Nurse?! I can't! I'm already in my hakama!

00:18:31.910 --> 00:18:33.260
Milk... I'll make some milk.

00:18:33.500 --> 00:18:35.940
Just hold on... Milk, milk...

00:18:37.460 --> 00:18:38.760
The hot water!

00:18:39.490 --> 00:18:40.670
The hot water...

00:18:39.800 --> 00:18:40.840
<b>Gone...</b>

00:18:41.290 --> 00:18:42.980
I'll ask for some more.

00:18:53.320 --> 00:18:55.300
J-Jin...

00:18:59.040 --> 00:19:00.300
Aki...

00:19:03.030 --> 00:19:08.240
<i>Is karuta... more important 
than my children?</i>

00:19:11.550 --> 00:19:14.510
I'm sorry, Jin and Aki.

00:19:14.510 --> 00:19:15.590
I'm sorry.

00:19:16.580 --> 00:19:17.310
Oh!

00:19:17.620 --> 00:19:20.130
You could go ahead and nurse him.

00:19:20.130 --> 00:19:20.560
Huh?

00:19:20.560 --> 00:19:22.470
B-But...

00:19:22.470 --> 00:19:26.370
Why do you think the kimono 
is open at the sides?

00:19:26.370 --> 00:19:29.270
Of course, it's not specifically 
for breastfeeding, but...

00:19:29.270 --> 00:19:30.420
Pardon me.

00:19:31.250 --> 00:19:33.860
Ah, they're so nice and soft.

00:19:33.860 --> 00:19:36.860
This should work just fine. 
Feed him through the opening.

00:19:40.710 --> 00:19:42.730
See? It's just fine.

00:19:42.730 --> 00:19:44.360
It won't even get wrinkled.

00:19:47.800 --> 00:19:50.000
Aren't kimono's convenient?

00:19:50.000 --> 00:19:51.900
They're a mother's best friend.

00:19:56.740 --> 00:19:59.250
U-Um... You are...

00:20:02.510 --> 00:20:08.100
<b>Oe Traditional Clothing
 Celebrating 120 years 
thanks to our customers</b>

00:20:05.420 --> 00:20:08.110
Feel free to call us whenever you need one!

00:20:08.100 --> 00:20:12.100
<b>Sh-She's a pro...           A kimono pro...</b>

00:20:09.290 --> 00:20:12.090
There you are, Mom! Where have you been?

00:20:12.830 --> 00:20:13.980
Oh, around.

00:20:13.980 --> 00:20:16.570
There's a girl in the Suihoku Society 
who has her coming-of-age soon.

00:20:16.570 --> 00:20:18.130
A business opportunity!

00:20:18.130 --> 00:20:19.120
You're fast!

00:20:19.350 --> 00:20:21.020
Mom!

00:20:23.820 --> 00:20:26.250
I'm sorry, Aki and Jin.

00:20:26.250 --> 00:20:27.130
Wait for me.

00:20:28.320 --> 00:20:31.710
I'm going to go become a queen.

00:20:32.370 --> 00:20:34.750
<b>Master and Queen Challenger Playoffs 

00:20:35.760 --> 00:20:39.010
<i>This is the day the challenger 
to the queen will be decided.</i>

00:20:41.010 --> 00:20:42.250
Ayase-senpai?!

00:20:42.260 --> 00:20:56.270
<b>Griiiiind</b>

00:20:42.510 --> 00:20:45.580
<i>I suddenly have intense regrets!</i>

00:20:45.580 --> 00:20:48.740
<i>Why am I not here as a competitor?!</i>

00:20:48.740 --> 00:20:52.800
<i>Mom! You might not remember
my first dream,</i>

00:20:52.800 --> 00:20:57.300
<i>but it wasn't to be a teacher! 
Not a teacher! Not a teacher!</i>

00:21:07.880 --> 00:21:08.990
My dream...

00:21:09.710 --> 00:21:12.580
I'm going to be a karuta master.

00:21:22.810 --> 00:21:23.920
It's time.

00:21:24.440 --> 00:21:26.360
All will be decided in a best-of-three.
